tgs:LinkNote.LimitsToGrowth_GayaHerrington a thinkr:LinkNote,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:aboutObject tgs:Persona.GayaHerrington ;
    thinkr:aboutSubject tgs:Concept.LimitsToGrowth ;
    thinkr:calculatedConfidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
    thinkr:hasEvidence tgs:Evidence.LimitsToGrowth_GayaHerrington ;
    skos:scopeNote "calculatedConfidence to be (re-)derived via scripts/compute_confidence.py, not hand-set. Arguably the strongest match surfaced across this whole extraction-pilot lineage (see the concept-mining prototype's own note on this exact case, scratchpad-only, not part of this repo): a direct, named, citable empirical update of the ORIGINAL Limits to Growth study, not a thematic echo. See this LinkNote's own header comment above for the real property-choice gap this case exposed."@en .

tgs:LinkNote.MartinLutherKingJr_GrowthImperative a thinkr:LinkNote,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:aboutObject tgs:Concept.GrowthImperative ;
    thinkr:aboutSubject tgs:Persona.MartinLutherKingJr ;
    thinkr:calculatedConfidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Curated ;
    thinkr:hasEvidence tgs:Evidence.MartinLutherKingJr_GrowthImperative ;
    skos:scopeNote "NAMING CAUGHT, SEMANTICS NOT YET REVIEWED (flagged 2026-07-15 during the LinkNote/Evidence/CrosswalkNote naming retrofit): aboutSubject/aboutObject here are REVERSED relative to every other LinkNote in this file — everywhere else a Concept is aboutSubject and a Persona/SchoolOfThought is aboutObject; here a Persona (MartinLutherKingJr) is aboutSubject and a Concept (GrowthImperative) is aboutObject. This individual's own local name is internally consistent with its own (possibly-backwards) properties — a plausible-looking name is NOT the same claim as a semantically-correct one. Deliberately NOT corrected as part of the naming retrofit (a rename task that also silently fixes semantics is a rename task that's hard to trust later) — needs its own deliberate review to determine whether aboutSubject/aboutObject should be swapped, or whether this one is intentionally different for a reason not yet documented. See docs/sidecar-cleanup-handoff.md's 2026-07-15 naming-retrofit entry."@en .

