tgs:LinkNote.Superorganism_JoshFarley a thinkr:LinkNote,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    thinkr:aboutObject tgs:Persona.JoshFarley ;
    thinkr:aboutSubject tgs:Concept.Superorganism ;
    thinkr:calculatedConfidence thinkr:ConfidenceType.Candidate ;
    thinkr:hasEvidence tgs:Evidence.Superorganism_JoshFarley,
        tgs:Evidence.Superorganism_JoshFarley_TGS_185 ;
    skos:scopeNote "calculatedConfidence correctly derived via scripts/compute_confidence.py (re-run 2026-07-15, see LinkNote.EnergyBlindness_ArtBerman's scopeNote for the stale-namespace bug this caught). Stays Candidate — both Evidence individuals are Candidate-confidence, not yet human-reviewed. This is the pilot's clearest example of the 'host-asserted explicit concept-connection' pattern the task was designed to test for (the Robert Lustig/Superorganism precedent discussed pre-pilot): Nate directly maps Farley's own thinking onto this Concept in his own words, not an inferred parallel."@en .

